# Every Java service Dockerfile does `COPY services/<module> services/<module>` from the repo root,
# then runs `mvn package` without a `clean` first. Without this file, a developer's own stale
# `target/` directory - compiled classes and resources from whatever the source tree looked like the
# last time they ran `mvn` on their host - gets copied straight into the build context and merged
# with the freshly-compiled output inside the container. A renamed or deleted source file (a Flyway
# migration, in particular - Flyway validates by filename, not content, so two files that both claim
# the same version number fail the build at startup) leaves its stale compiled copy behind, and no
# --no-cache rebuild fixes it, because the contamination is in the build context Docker reads from,
# not in Docker's own layer cache.
target/
**/target/

# The frontend dashboard is built fresh inside the Docker build (frontend-maven-plugin's -Pui
# profile), never from a pre-built host copy - a stale host dist/ or a host-installed node_modules
# (often built for the host's OS/architecture, not the container's) must not leak in either.
frontend/sfl-operations-ui/node_modules/
frontend/sfl-operations-ui/dist/

# Editor/VCS/OS noise that never belongs in a build context.
.git/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Runtime configuration, credentials and local-only state must never enter an image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
uploads/
**/uploads/
# Do not exclude a generic `vendor/` directory: Facilities has Java packages under
# `shared/application/vendor/` that are required by the compile.
outputs/
**/outputs/
.mcp.json
